# Subvert - the acid line, and the rest of what the filter can do.
#
# Thirteen parameters, and eight of them are one idea: a resonant filter with
# an envelope thrown at it. So this bank is not a tour of the panel, it is a
# tour of that one idea - how far open, how much envelope, how fast it shuts -
# and then the four controls that are not part of it: the sub, the pulse
# width, the band-pass mode and the drive.
#
# Levelled to about -8 dB RMS against each other, so the bank does not change
# volume as you walk down it. Two sit below that and both earn it: Band
# Squelch is band-passed, so most of the spectrum is gone and its volume is
# already at the top, and Doorstop is a thud - a high crest factor is what it
# is for. Values are in each parameter's own units; `audition params Subvert`
# lists them.

machine Subvert
role    bass

patch Init

patch Classic
  # The one everybody means. Open enough to hear the note, resonant enough to
  # hear the filter, and a decay that shuts before the next eighth.
  #
  # Further from the machine's own defaults than it first was: at 520 Hz and
  # 0.62 it measured the same as Init, and a bank whose first two entries are
  # the same sound has nine patches in it, not ten.
  cutoff         410 Hz
  resonance      0.72
  envmod         0.64
  decay          280 ms
  accent         0.75
  slide          50 ms
  drive          0.16

patch Squelch
  # Further into the resonance and a much faster decay: the blip rather than
  # the sweep. Accent nearly all the way up, because on a line like this the
  # accented steps are the line.
  cutoff         330 Hz
  resonance      0.9
  envmod         0.85
  decay          130 ms
  accent         0.92
  slide          40 ms
  drive          0.22
  volume         0.72

patch Rubber
  # A pulse instead of a saw, wide slide, and enough drive to round the peak
  # off. The one that bends between notes rather than stepping.
  wave           #1
  pw             0.42
  cutoff         295 Hz
  resonance      0.75
  envmod         0.7
  decay          150 ms
  accent         0.8
  slide          130 ms
  drive          0.25
  volume         0.6

patch "Long Sweep"
  # A decay far longer than a step, so the filter never closes and the line
  # rises across the bar instead of inside each note.
  cutoff         180 Hz
  resonance      0.72
  envmod         0.95
  decay          1600 ms
  accent         0.45
  slide          60 ms
  drive          0.15
  volume         0.72

patch "Sub Hollow"
  # The sub is the note and the pulse is the edge on it. Narrow width, filter
  # low, very little envelope: a bass that stays where it is put.
  wave           #1
  pw             0.24
  sub            0.65
  cutoff         220 Hz
  resonance      0.38
  envmod         0.3
  decay          480 ms
  accent         0.5
  drive          0.08
  volume         0.7

patch "Band Squelch"
  # Band-pass: no bottom and no top, so what is left is the resonance itself.
  # Volume at the top and drive doing the rest, and it is still the quietest
  # thing here by two decibels - which is what taking the ends off a spectrum
  # costs, not something to pretend away.
  mode           #1
  cutoff         690 Hz
  resonance      0.85
  envmod         0.8
  decay          120 ms
  accent         0.9
  drive          0.55
  volume         1

patch Buzzsaw
  # Filter nearly out of the way and the drive doing the work. Not acid at
  # all - the machine's other end, and the reason drive is in the voice
  # rather than in an insert.
  cutoff         3200 Hz
  resonance      0.25
  envmod         0.25
  decay          400 ms
  accent         0.55
  drive          0.85
  volume         0.92

patch "Thin Ice"
  # Right at the top of the resonance with almost no envelope: it whistles on
  # the note rather than under it. The one that shows resonance is a tone.
  cutoff         1400 Hz
  resonance      0.97
  envmod         0.15
  decay          220 ms
  accent         0.4
  drive          0.05
  volume         0.85

patch Doorstop
  # Shut. Almost no cutoff, almost all envelope, and a decay short enough
  # that each note is a thud with a pitch somewhere inside it.
  cutoff         90 Hz
  resonance      0.55
  envmod         1
  decay          90 ms
  accent         0.85
  slide          25 ms
  drive          0.3
  volume         0.85
